  "id": "Compound::DB05271 - Gene::151",
  "verbalization": "Rotigotine is implicated in the regulation of Adra2b through a shared mechanism involving Lisuride, which binds to Adra2b. Both Rotigotine and Lisuride are classified as agents affecting the nervous system and as organic molecular entities, suggesting a common pathway in their interaction with Adra2b. The evidence from the two paths indicates that Rotigotine causes either Sudden Onset Of Sleep or Binge Eating, both of which are mediated by Lisuride, which in turn binds to Adra2b. This suggests that the interaction between Rotigotine and Adra2b is indirectly mediated through Lisuride, with the two entities sharing a common biological role in the nervous system. The integration of these findings highlights a potential mechanism by which Rotigotine influences Adra2b, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
